{
  "$comment": [
    "Dashboard colour themes. To add a theme, copy any block below, give it a unique id,",
    "and change the colours. Nothing else needs editing - the theme picker builds itself",
    "from this file at page load.",
    "",
    "  id           unique key, also what gets saved in the browser",
    "  name         what appears in the theme dropdown",
    "  type         'dark' or 'light' - only affects default shadows and a few UI accents",
    "  colors       every value is a plain CSS colour (hex, rgb(), hsl() - anything CSS accepts)",
    "",
    "Colour roles:",
    "  bg             page background",
    "  panel          card / table background",
    "  panelAlt       striped rows, hover states",
    "  textPrimary    body text",
    "  textSecondary  labels, captions, muted text",
    "  border         card borders, table rules",
    "  headerFrom     header gradient start (use the same as headerTo for a flat header)",
    "  headerTo       header gradient end",
    "  headerText     text on the header",
    "  navLink        nav links and accents",
    "  navLinkHover   nav link hover",
    "  chartPrimary   main chart series",
    "  chartSecondary second chart series",
    "  chartSuccess   healthy / under threshold",
    "  chartWarning   warning threshold",
    "  chartDanger    critical threshold / over quota",
    "  chartMuted     gridlines, empty states"
  ],

